So, it's there's

00:45:15.635 --> 00:45:17.075
a fair bit of discretion.

00:45:19.610 --> 00:45:23.450
So first of all, we use a professional weather forecasting

00:45:24.330 --> 00:45:25.450
service

00:45:25.450 --> 00:45:26.410
that's

00:45:26.490 --> 00:45:28.570
specifically for public works,

00:45:29.770 --> 00:45:31.530
both for alerts

00:45:31.530 --> 00:45:32.730
and for

00:45:32.810 --> 00:45:34.650
doing a better job of forecasting

00:45:35.125 --> 00:45:41.045
when we're actually going to have snow on the ground, what the pavement temperatures are likely to be, and what's needed.

00:45:41.845 --> 00:45:46.085
And we very carefully vary the amount of salt we put down

00:45:46.645 --> 00:45:51.510
when we plow and when we salt kind of based on what's expected.

00:45:51.910 --> 00:45:54.710
So, don't think there's, I can't give you a,

00:45:55.190 --> 00:45:56.390
after

00:45:56.390 --> 00:46:00.470
a half inch we do this because it's very temperature dependent.

00:46:02.870 --> 00:46:12.285
Like for instance, you don't go down and put salt down before a snowstorm because then as people drive over it, it just gets bounced off the road and it doesn't do you any good.

00:46:13.405 --> 00:46:19.165
Usually right after it snows the first pass you salt only, you don't put the plows down

00:46:19.750 --> 00:46:24.950
and you wait till you get about an inch or two, sometimes three inches of snow before you plow.

00:46:25.110 --> 00:46:28.710
Because what you want to do is you want to melt that lowest layer

00:46:28.790 --> 00:46:31.270
so it never adheres to the roadway.

00:46:31.750 --> 00:46:33.590
But that's also temperature dependent.

00:46:34.375 --> 00:46:38.855
And we're also starting to buy both treated and untreated salt,

00:46:39.015 --> 00:46:41.415
because the price of treated salt has

00:46:41.655 --> 00:46:43.095
gotten much higher.

00:46:45.255 --> 00:46:51.730
You know, and we're going to start putting down either treated or untreated salt based on the temperature conditions,

00:46:51.730 --> 00:46:54.850
because treated salt works at a much lower temperature

00:46:54.930 --> 00:46:56.610
than untreated salt.

00:46:56.850 --> 00:46:57.570
So I

00:46:58.130 --> 00:47:01.650
